<title>UK: UK NOTES IN CIRCULATION RISE 5.8% WEEK TO AUGUST 6.</title>
<headline>UK NOTES IN CIRCULATION RISE 5.8% WEEK TO AUGUST 6.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>British bank notes in circulation rose 5.8 percent in the week to August 6 over the equivalent week a year ago, the Bank of England said on Thursday. Last week the rise was 5.6 percent.</p>
<p>(Figures in rounded billions of stg)</p>
<p>			  Latest week   Previous wk   Year-ago wk</p>
<p>Notes in circulation  22.10	   22.05	   20.89</p>
<p>Bankers deposits	 2.51	    2.61	    1.97</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom 44 171 542 2774</p>
</text>
